Define DataTable Variables in UiPath

A DataTable variable in UiPath is a special type of variable used to store and manage data in
a tabular format consisting of rows and columns, similar to an Excel worksheet or a database table.

A DataTable can store multiple records together instead of storing each value in separate variables.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Organization of Data

In a DataTable:

Columns represent the categories or fields of information.
Rows represent individual records or entries.

Example:

Employee ID	Name	Department
101	Harini	AI & DS
102	Rahul	CSE
103	Priya	IT

Here:

Employee ID, Name, Department are columns.
Each employee record is stored in a separate row.
----------------------------------------------------------
Importance of DataTable Variables

Store Large Amounts of Structured Data
 DataTables can store multiple records in a single variable.

Manage Data Efficiently
 They allow sorting, filtering, updating, and deleting data easily.

Transfer Data Between Applications
 Data can be read from Excel, databases, or websites and then written to another application.

Support Data Processing
 They are useful for generating reports, analyzing information, and performing calculations.

Enable Data Migration
 DataTables help transfer data from one system to another without losing structure.
